You don't need to check if you can pray safely if:

You know that it has been a reasonable time since you prayed &
You have a problem that your god can solve.

Or

You know you've pissed off your god.


One good example:

You start a new game and kill monsters (= alignment is positive). You 
get hungry and cannot find any food. When you get weak you pray and your 
god fills your stomach.

Now, you can rely on the fact that if you don't pray and you don't do 
anything that might upset your god, she will fill your stomach the next 
time you get weak if you pray.


One must remember that one only prays to god for help, unless one stands 
on an altar. And if you stand on a coaligned altar then its trivial to 
check if one can pray.

So, summa summarum: From start of the game pray only if you are in 
trouble. When ever you are at a coaligned altar sacrifice so that when 
you continue you know you can pray. Outside altars pray only in dire 
straits.

